### **6.5 Automated Combinatorial Test Generation**

**The Problem**: Manually creating combinatorial test cases is **error-prone** and **time-consuming**.

**The Solution**: Use tools to **automatically generate** optimal test cases.

---

#### **Tools for Combinatorial Test Generation**

**1. Microsoft PICT (Pairwise Independent Combinatorial Testing)**
- **URL**: https://github.com/Microsoft/pict
- **License**: MIT (Free)
- **Platform**: Windows, Linux, macOS
- **Use Case**: Generate pairwise test cases for any parameter combination

**2. ACTS (Advanced Combinatorial Testing System)**
- **URL**: https://csrc.nist.gov/projects/automated-combinatorial-testing-for-software
- **License**: Public domain
- **Platform**: Java-based (cross-platform)
- **Use Case**: Complex constraints and t-way testing (pairwise, 3-way, 4-way)

**3. jenny (Java-based combinatorial tool)**
- **URL**: https://burtleburtle.net/bob/math/jenny.html
- **License**: Public domain
- **Platform**: Cross-platform
- **Use Case**: Lightweight pairwise testing

