### **The 80/20 Rule of Testing**

#### **Why 95% is the Optimal Target**

**Research Finding**: Pairwise testing (2-way) is the **"sweet spot"** for cost-effectiveness.

| Coverage Level | Test Cases Required | Defects Found | Cost-Benefit |
|---------------|-------------------|---------------|--------------|
| **Exhaustive** | 10,000+ tests | 100% | ❌ Impractical |
| **4-way** | ~1,000 tests | 99.9% | ❌ 100x effort for 4.9% more |
| **3-way** | ~200 tests | 98-99% | ⚠️ 20x effort for 4% more |
| **2-way (Pairwise)** | ~46 tests | **90-95%** | ✅ **OPTIMAL** |
| **Ad-hoc** | ~10 tests | 50-60% | ❌ Insufficient |

**Key Insight**: Going from **95% → 99%** coverage requires **10-20x more tests** but only finds **4% more defects**.

