## Conclusion

**Comprehensive testing is not optional**. Every test suite MUST include these **5 core categories**:
1. ✅ Positive tests (happy path)
2. ✅ Negative tests (error handling)
3. ✅ Edge cases (boundary conditions)
4. ✅ Functional tests (business rules & workflows, ≥50 FIXED)
5. ✅ Integration tests (end-to-end data flows, ≥50 FIXED)

And these **additional mandatory categories**:
6. ✅ Concurrency tests (race conditions, ≥25 FIXED)
7. ✅ Unit tests (≥21 FIXED)
8. ✅ Performance tests (≥16 FIXED)
9. ✅ Load tests (≥10 FIXED)

> **Security testing is OUT OF SCOPE for the QA team.** Do **not** create `SecurityTests.cs` by default. Security testing is handled separately by Infrastructure and Security teams. See `QA Tests/Test Plans/SECURITY_TESTING_QUESTIONNAIRE.md`.

**No exceptions**. No "we'll add it later". No "it's just a small feature".

**Comprehensive from day 1. Every time. No compromise.**

